WEBVTT

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:40.890
To become a beastinarian for beast-lords, Erin came to the Kazalm Beast-Lord Care Center.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:49.930
Erin passed the Trial of the Entrees and was admitted to the second year of Junior High.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:57.600
Erin parted with Jone and started to walk her own path.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.380
It's morning.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:17.070
It's a beast-lord!

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:34.990
I wonder why...

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:40.880
The beast-lords here are different from the ones I've seen before.

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:48.710
Why?

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:57.700
Friends at Kazalm

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.800
Erin!

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.040
Erin!

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:06.920
So this is where you were.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.760
Yeah, since I wanted to see the beast-lords.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:11.940
Forget that.  You have to get ready fast.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.360
It's time for breakfast.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.620
We've got to hurry!

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:25.210
Hey, where are those two?

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.170
Sorry we're late!

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:38.960
Yuuyan!  How many years have you been here?

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.720
I'm really sorry.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.790
Come for your meals on time!

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:44.120
You know that, right?

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:47.260
Seriously, cut me some slack.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:50.020
Um, Yuuyan didn't do anything wrong.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:52.310
I'm the reason for coming late.

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:54.570
I'm really sorry.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:00.240
You'd better watch out from now on.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:07.980
She's really strict with time, but she's a nice person.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:11.480
This way please, princesses.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.440
Oh please, calling us princesses?

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.680
Girls are all princesses.

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:21.910
Hey, your belt knot is wrong again.

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:24.200
Doesn't that make me unique?

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:28.000
Erin, this is Kashugan.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.020
Nice to meet you.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:33.590
Across from us are Wooly and Urari.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:37.120
Over there is Tyna,

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:38.760
Tamarin,

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.090
Chaman,

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:41.300
Panche and

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.460
Hanuka.

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:44.830
I'm Erin.

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:46.600
Nice to meet you all.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:48.600
Let's see...

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.120
Kashugan and...

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.310
Wooly and...

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.630
Urari and...

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.110
Well, nobody expects you to remember them all at once.

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:00.600
So, let's eat.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:02.620
Itadakimasu.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:08.610
What's this?

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.500
It's a taichi.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:11.740
"Taichi?"

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:14.200
It's a really delicious fruit.

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:16.490
Really?

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:17.750
No, don't!

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.120
You have to peel the skin off.

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:23.030
It's bitter!

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:30.160
It's sour...

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:32.980
That's 'cause you gulped down the asera juice...

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:38.960
Looks like there are lots of things for us to teach you despite you being a meritocrat.

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:58.510
Good morning.  There's great weather today, isn't there?

00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:00.330
Good morning!

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:03.800
Good morning!

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.250
You must be the new student.

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:11.040
It's good to see that you're filled with enthusiasm.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:16.460
All right, today, we'll talk about bird anatomy.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:20.310
Take a look at the figure on page 25.

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:26.680
All birds, as well as beast-lords, have very developed breast muscles.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:32.640
Without these developed breast muscles, they wouldn't be able to flap those large wings.

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:36.360
However, the beast-lords here cannot fly.

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:41.140
We don't know why they can't fly.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.820
What's the matter?  Do you have a question?

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:48.540
What do you mean by saying beast-lords can't fly?

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:54.310
Beast-lords that have been in the care of humans from infancy can't fly.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:07:00.080
Why can't they fly if they've been in care of humans from infancy?

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:02.120
Are you restraining them from flying?

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:04.880
That's not true.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:10.770
It's not only the beast-lords here, but those in the capital can't fly, either.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:12.930
How come?

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:17.550
What's the difference between the wild beast-lords and the beast-lords at Kazalm?

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:20.040
Is there a difference in how they're raised?

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.930
That's enough!

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:24.950
Now is not the time to learn about beast-lords.

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:28.420
Plus, this isn't a private lesson for you.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:36.140
I'm sorry.

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:42.610
That's the north building.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.340
Over there is the practical field.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:48.920
And here is the atrium.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:52.600
There's a library inside, too.

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:53.770
"Library?"

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:05.240
Erin!  If we don't hurry, the practical's going to start!

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:06.890
Ah, right.

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:12.430
You must not eat summer bells.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:14.100
Make a good note of it,

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:14.890
all of you.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:17.380
Hey, you.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:18.670
You!

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:19.640
Hey, you!

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:20.860
Yes.

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:26.420
If you're like that as a transfer, you won't be able to follow the classes.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.440
I'm sorry.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.850
Okay, back to class.

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:35.770
Who here knows how a summer bell can be utilized?

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:39.100
Here.  The nectar is poisonous.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:46.410
But in the <i>Book of Poisons</i>, it's said to help alleviate anxiety and mental disorders if boiled.

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:53.020
However, too much intake can cause perspiration and an increase in blood pressure.

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:59.060
T-That's something you learn in college.

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:00.950
Wow.

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:02.910
Pure luck.

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:13.420
To Erin, this new place, Kazalm, was a very exciting place.

00:09:13.420 --> 00:09:21.820
However, coming from a life of living in the mountains with Jone, she couldn't follow the rules.

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:28.140
Where did Erin go?

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:32.720
It's already lunch.  She sure gives us a lot of trouble.

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:35.690
Maybe she's lost somewhere?

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:38.000
Everyone, come search for her with me.

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:40.760
Why us, too?

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.900
She's our new buddy!

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:45.060
Stop complaining and let's find her!

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:52.030
I guess she's not in the classroom.

00:09:52.030 --> 00:09:54.410
Seriously, where did she go?

00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:59.130
What's the matter, all of you?

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:08.600
You were absorbed with reading the books in the library?

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:10.710
Yes...

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:17.500
Refrain from self-indulgent acts while living communally.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:19.960
Everyone will get worried, right?

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:21.200
You understand, right?

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:24.630
Yes.  I'm sorry.

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:25.940
Esal-sensei.

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:29.060
I'd like to ask you something regarding Lilan.

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:33.480
Very well.  Come to my office.

00:10:38.270 --> 00:10:41.480
Transfer students have it rough, getting all the attention, don't they?

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:43.820
Give it your best.

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:46.250
Thank you very much.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.580
Now that's Tomura-senpai.

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:51.650
He's got such a great presence.

00:10:53.810 --> 00:11:01.740
Erin became aware once again that here, she must walk alongside everyone else.

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:10.720
To live communally, this was something Erin had never experienced.

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:19.880
Be on time for the meals.

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:23.140
Don't ask anything that's not directly related to the class.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:26.570
Don't perform any self-indulgent acts.

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:45.110
You can have mine.

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:48.980
Don't push things you don't like onto me!

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:52.190
You know you can't be loud during meal times!

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:02.880
What are you staring at my face for?

00:12:03.650 --> 00:12:06.210
No!  It's nothing!

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:10.410
It's sour!

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:16.400
Kochichi weed and chichi mimic can be differentiated by how they grow.

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:19.230
You.  You seem to be listening today.

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:19.900
Yes.

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:41.820
There's something I wanted to bring up to you all.

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:43.440
What is it?

00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:45.900
It's about Erin.

00:13:46.390 --> 00:13:49.680
Don't you all think her enthusiasm's gone?

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:07.990
Yuuyan.

00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:11.420
Erin, can I have a moment of your time?

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:13.390
I want you to come with me.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:31.330
Welcome, Erin-chan!

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:34.190
What is this?

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:36.080
Your welcome party!

00:14:37.220 --> 00:14:41.550
We should have done it sooner.  Sorry it's so late.

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:51.070
We want you to know more about us, and we all want to know more about you.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:53.230
Thank you!

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:55.190
Now, Urari-kun!

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:57.400
Word of welcome please!

00:14:57.400 --> 00:15:06.200
Erm, here at Kazalm Beast-Lord Care Center, students gather from all around in pursuit of becoming a beastinarian.

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:15.200
This place runs upon money provided by the Queen, and we do not have to pay any tuition.

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:21.340
Therefore the admission test is very strict, and since we passed that, we are the chosen ones, thus-

00:15:21.340 --> 00:15:24.170
Anyways, congratulations on entering!

00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:26.660
I'm still speaking!

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:29.240
Would you like a dance with me?

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:30.780
Sounds good!

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:32.600
We'll dance as well!

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:39.810
What's wrong, Kashugan?

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:42.220
She's asleep.

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:43.460
No way.

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:48.750
E-Erin.

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:53.000
Be on time for the meals...

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:56.090
Don't ask anything that's not directly related to the class...

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:13.780
I thought you'd stay asleep until morning.

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:17.060
Here, have some tea.

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:20.320
I...

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:22.480
I fell asleep?!

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:24.390
Yeah.

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:30.110
What should I do, when everyone got the event together for me?

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:32.470
I'll go apologize to everyone!

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:34.340
They're not bothered by it.

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:35.850
But!

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:38.240
We're more worried about you!

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:41.720
It looks like you're pushing yourself.

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:44.830
Do you have something that's troubling you?

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:55.810
How I have to act like everyone else.

00:16:57.220 --> 00:17:00.460
Unlike everyone else, I'm strange.

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:04.380
But I don't have a place to go home to anymore.

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:08.160
So I have to be the same as everyone else.

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:13.290
Note: Yuuyan speaks with an Osaka-based dialect.
If you say so, but do you see how I speak?

00:17:13.290 --> 00:17:16.460
People laughed at me a lot when I had just started.

00:17:16.460 --> 00:17:16.960
Note: Yuuyan speaks with an Osaka-based dialect.

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:21.600
I thought I had to talk like everyone else did, too.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:26.010
So then, you know, that Kashugan...

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:30.060
The person who always ties his belt knot wrong?

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:33.860
Yeah.  He spoke up to everyone.

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:39.000
"Someone's dialect depends on where they come from.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:44.720
You wouldn't want your dialect laughed at, would you?"

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:48.550
We're all different.

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:53.290
That's why I won't ignore the fact that you're of the Mist People, either.

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:58.440
It's human nature to wonder about things that are different from their own.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:03.210
Be it "strange" or "of the Mist People," you are who you are, Erin.

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:07.810
The Erin who's as cute as an apple blossom when she laughs.

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:18.350
Since she was little, the fact that she was of the Mist People was a prick to her heart.

00:18:19.420 --> 00:18:25.830
This was the first time Erin felt that it was all right to be different.

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:30.340
What's the matter?

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:36.290
Thank you, Yuuyan.

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:43.280
You're making me cry, too.

00:18:49.760 --> 00:18:54.240
I hope we can always smile at each other like this.

00:18:54.790 --> 00:18:55.660
Yeah.

00:18:57.590 --> 00:19:01.770
Hey, Yuuyan.  I want to apologize to everyone.

00:19:01.770 --> 00:19:02.790
So...

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:11.560
Everyone!  Wake your butts up!

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:14.350
What are you doing so early in the morning?

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:16.330
What happened?

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:18.550
Erin's calling you all.

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:27.000
Erin!  I brought everyone!

00:19:29.260 --> 00:19:30.720
Kashugan.

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:31.700
Wooly.

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:33.140
Urari.

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:34.780
Tyna.

00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:36.270
Hanuka.

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:37.630
Panche.

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:41.140
And Tamarin and Chaman.

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:44.120
I'm sorry about last night!

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:48.250
She got all of our names down.

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:54.060
As an apology, I'll give my hospitality to everyone today.

00:19:54.660 --> 00:19:58.070
I've prepared some fresh fruit juice and honey.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:06.390
It's the honey I made when I was living with a honey man before coming here.

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:07.930
Really?

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.350
Please enjoy.

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:14.500
It looks delicious!

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:28.160
It's sweet!

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:30.130
It's like it's melting!

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:31.270
Isn't it?

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:36.990
Also, the reason why I had you all come so early is,

00:20:36.990 --> 00:20:40.660
because I wanted you all to see the beast-lords from here.

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:58.490
You woke us up for something like this?

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:02.630
We see beast-lords everyday.

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:05.790
Though, the beast-lords here are always sleeping.

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:09.020
Yeah, they're lazy.

00:21:09.020 --> 00:21:10.830
I'm still sleepy.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:13.820
What?  Did I...

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:19.040
But it's very typical of Erin.

00:21:19.510 --> 00:21:21.950
I couldn't even bring myself to yell at her.

00:21:21.950 --> 00:21:24.750
We're starting to understand your personality.

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:28.240
Beast-lord gung-ho?

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:29.970
That's it.

00:21:31.070 --> 00:21:33.360
"Beast-lord gung-ho?"

00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:35.990
That fits you perfectly!

00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:43.920
It's Tomura-senpai!

00:21:44.270 --> 00:21:46.380
Tomura-senpai!

00:21:49.260 --> 00:21:52.090
Tomura-senpai's amazing, don't you think?

00:21:52.090 --> 00:21:57.610
He's still a student, yet he's taking care of a baby beast-lord.

00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:00.320
"Baby beast-lord?"

00:22:03.730 --> 00:22:05.220
A baby beast-lord.

00:22:05.990 --> 00:22:12.330
Hearing that reminded Erin of the beast-lord family at Mt. Kasho.

00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:22.620
She was remembering the beautiful figures of the cute baby and the parent that was embracing it.

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:04.220
Kazalm is filled with beast-lords.

00:24:04.570 --> 00:24:09.420
I want to take care of beast-lords soon as well, but I don't want to use the mute whistle.

00:24:09.420 --> 00:24:13.470
At Kazalm, there is a young, wounded beast-lord.

00:24:13.470 --> 00:24:18.190
It's separated from its mother and is shivering in fear in the dark.

00:24:18.540 --> 00:24:20.430
I want to do something for it.

00:24:21.420 --> 00:24:25.050
Kemono no Souja Erin.  The Beast-Lord Named Lilan.

00:24:25.050 --> 00:24:30.030
The Beast-Lord Named Lilan.
